                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.4/208: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-29T13:00:00+01:00">July 29, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 29—9:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>230. Department’s 148, July 2, 5 p.m. Informal assurances received that the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">President Fillmore</hi> will not be subjected to the
                    requirement in question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
